# Line endings.  The index already stores LF for these paths; the Linux
# toolchain in the dev container (GNU make, /bin/sh) additionally needs LF on
# disk, so pin them at checkout as well.
#
# Deliberately no `* text=auto`: it would renormalize committed originals that
# are stored CRLF byte-for-byte (see the -text rows below).
Makefile text eol=lf
makefile text eol=lf
GNUmakefile text eol=lf
*.mk text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.dockerignore text eol=lf
compose.yaml text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Extracted inputs are byte-exact as shipped (the index stores them with CRLF);
# keep git from converting or renormalizing them, so `git add --renormalize .`
# can never corrupt an oracle input.
extracted/ORDER.FRM -text
extracted/ORDERFRM.TXT -text
extracted/VENDOR.DOC -text
